From bf3dadc74e53136d593fd993bc8ebd138c808a1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Swapnil Raj <raj.swapnil99@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 16:52:09 +0000
Subject: fix: correct Blake3 MSG_SCHEDULE and add independent tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous MSG_SCHEDULE for rounds 3-6 was wrong — it matched neither
the official Blake3 reference nor the permutation formula
schedule[r][j] = schedule[r-1][PERM[j]]. This meant the precompile
proved a self-consistent but non-standard computation.

Fix all three copies (machine chip, tracing executor, minimal executor)
to use the correct table from the Blake3 spec / blake3 crate.

Also strengthen the test suite with three fast unit tests:
- test_msg_schedule_formula: verifies the table matches the permutation
  formula independently
- test_compress_vs_blake3_crate: runs compress_inner_ref on 4 different
  64-byte inputs and checks the XOR output matches blake3::hash (the
  official crate used as oracle)
- test_chip_msg_schedule_matches_spec: asserts the machine chip constant
  matches the independently-verified reference table

The proof test now uses hardcoded reference constants (not imported from
the machine chip) so a bug in the chip's table would cause a failure.

